Now I'll add tests. I need a way to build a frame with shared subtree. The music player pattern: `View shared = ...; View wide = HStack.children(shared, sidebar); View compact = HStack.children(shared);` Then SizeThatFits.make(Fit.of(wide, 1024), Fit.of(compact)). This does NOT reuse the same instance as candidates (wide != compact), so it passes rejection. But `shared` is used inside both. In snapshot emission, `wide.render` and `compact.render` each render `shared` → distinct nodes. Good.

